       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**, three times the maximum recommended daily dose. The FDA-labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. At 7,650 mg/day the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is serious, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\n**My guess at what you meant:** 2,550 mg is the total daily dose, so the order would be **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**.\n\nCould you tell me which of these you want?\n1. **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day), or\n2. A different dose, such as a lower starting dose (for example, 500 mg BID or 850 mg daily, titrated up), or\n3. Exactly 2550 mg per dose TID, if that's intended. I'd need you to confirm it explicitly.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
